		{
			dependencies: ["0B15042E60AEDA3D"]
			description: [
				"It's time to do some mining. There are two options, the vastly more resource efficient &bGregTech&r veins or the familiar caving."
				""
				"Unlike standard &bGregTech&r, &avanilla ore veins still generate&r. Caving is still a viable activity in the early game for getting yourself established while your resource stockpiles are low."
				""
				"Whatever you decide to do, report back once you have a stack of Cobblestone."
				""
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"For the uninitiated, &bGregTech&r ore veins are large ore deposits that spawn ores of a specific type. They generate at varying Y levels, &cbut always generate at the center of every 3 chunks in any given world.&r They are marked by piles of dust on the surface. Digging straight down in the center of a chunk where these appear will lead you to the corresponding ore vein. These ore veins are automatically marked on your map, and you can craft ore prospectors later on that show you a view of what ore veins are around you."
			]
			id: "1D81C6B949B81B63"
			subtitle: "First half of the name comes second."
			tasks: [{
				id: "50F94BFE4035D3B3"
				item: "minecraft:cobblestone"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "Mining"
			x: 7.5d
			y: 1.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["6E74ACFF47D62C68"]
			description: ["Iron is still as useful as ever, be sure to make plenty."]
